body:
@mkouba I will answer each question one at a time:

1. In this particular case, that filter is used to serve the FE (Angular app). I followed this official documentation from [here](https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-and-web-ui-development-mode/). 
```
@WebFilter(urlPatterns = "/*", asyncSupported = true)
@Priority(value = 300)
public class AngularResourcesFilter extends HttpFilter {
// code
}
```
But this is not the only source of exception. Other filters also throw this. 
2. It doesn't need. I removed @ApplicationScoped but this not fixed my issue
3. Indeed, using `quarkus.arc.dev-mode.monitoring-enabled=false` temporary fix my issue. 

 My hunch says that it is a filter chain issue.
